[{:db/id 17592186073898 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7c0b31cd-a8d3-5683-9fdd-277be817d76f" "question-1e30d664-9e23-51db-b1eb-ca432067421a" "question-3fc543bd-aabf-514b-90ee-2a0e14116a62" "question-6ea34bb6-0171-5294-84a0-af7868985cc0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073587 :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(2,4)$  and $(5,4)?$\n\n![](images/ce/ce70a8122559f67aac379349fb369e6e7e007e85fa8a13632e7865469804fb6a.png)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/bd/bd568e789e79574225dbd75e79d4cacb2fbf92beb048f5bdafeb67f74ab029f6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/fb/fb2f075f8321aca3823770e28a86a8d9532cb343ba4239f94c2fb9d1cc883b0b.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{5}},4)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{5}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{2}},4)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{2}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{blue}{5}} - {\\color{red}{2}} = 3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073899 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e3f03e2a-4bac-5cce-92a0-e7b608f8a540" "question-0b4b4ad6-a121-56c5-9ffb-f11907c80995" "question-059dbb93-56f4-55ee-894b-e3361b03f75b" "question-fa03ff7a-210e-5a15-a83d-9725f208427d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073588 :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-4,-2)$  and $(-4,-5)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/0d/0d26dd64fad1809f58fecdf802a28b5ab6d1dd201b63dc0bb9293f248a127a85.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/fb/fbc52312edf77508a9d7436acd515bc91e3225826c16b85c3571143c39886771.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/80/80be7ec0ed67ce819b51b34f7a50aeb51786e3a6ca9190b418b2ec96e127cc78.png)\n\nThe point $(-4,{\\color{red}{-5}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{5}$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-4,{\\color{blue}{-2}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{2}$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{5}} - {\\color{blue}{2}} = 3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073900 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1c563b17-7efa-524a-b66b-42f86b7b1c69" "question-58108774-1bb4-55a8-baca-82691653ff84" "question-6eda6b89-4c3a-5cda-b0b9-3c5028cd27fb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073589 :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(3,4)$  and $(3,-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/47/47f203755bf0abcbf33be636331e4f9c0119c14620f1a658be31db0d6feeed17.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $7$ units, so the distance equals $7.$\n\n![](images/79/79b944cc0d1af7577282653e3250af844ad10256bb3b6cf2b204ed2f9862d480.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/94/94a5e438b160ce6f3dca0f44fd418a8831c520543e7dad605ea23674500af5fd.png)\n\nThe point $(3,{\\color{blue}{4}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{4}$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(3,{\\color{red}{-3}})$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{3}$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{3}} + {\\color{blue}{4}} = 7.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186074463 :question/problem "![](images/91/91babd6196f0a16bcaf052af27218e9e96ef5bc3d49c0ea46014ac9ba9737b86.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(1,3)$  and $(5,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/b4/b46f87399fc02d2d63199bee5f7a584c067adaf7526c085614c4e124118aae06.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/0f/0f2c7b0dc5aafa14501aec735c74b21cc653a0b9799ff55e204fe8f8d530e1ce.png)\n\nThe point $(5,3)$ is at a distance of $5$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(1,3)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $5-1=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073016 :answer-field/correct 17592186073018 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c0b31cd-a8d3-5683-9fdd-277be817d76f" :question/id #uuid "7c0b31cd-a8d3-5683-9fdd-277be817d76f" :question/math-academy-id "q-160270" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(2,-1)$  and $(4,-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/52/52ecfaaa72633fd76cca857b65ada4fb8238822bbe51fed4f913ecf41753e378.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $2$ units, so the distance equals $2.$\n\n![](images/59/59ec31381dd594b4219dd89dfff899d8d937bfff40b41280e21575c505a4feba.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/f7/f7ed15e2eb21768de1db6e60694dcacdbcc9072f425170e990f1bb32295f9f46.png)\n\nThe point $(2,-1)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(4,-1)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4-2=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-180fce76-a687-500d-9ca0-f63a7c176ee5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-180fce76-a687-500d-9ca0-f63a7c176ee5" :answer-field/id #uuid "180fce76-a687-500d-9ca0-f63a7c176ee5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b8d75d7-8abf-54f9-8f4b-b51aaf637278" :answer-field/choices ["answer-511bfc21-c221-53ff-9dd6-6d4d9075e785" "answer-0b8d75d7-8abf-54f9-8f4b-b51aaf637278" "answer-b053775f-2f4b-59e7-a5fb-41ee02174a56" "answer-1784e63d-58ba-553a-8287-ebb64594c0a5" "answer-119bb1ed-0657-5ae4-90f2-e955e4848fbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-511bfc21-c221-53ff-9dd6-6d4d9075e785" :answer/id #uuid "511bfc21-c221-53ff-9dd6-6d4d9075e785" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b8d75d7-8abf-54f9-8f4b-b51aaf637278" :answer/id #uuid "0b8d75d7-8abf-54f9-8f4b-b51aaf637278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b053775f-2f4b-59e7-a5fb-41ee02174a56" :answer/id #uuid "b053775f-2f4b-59e7-a5fb-41ee02174a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1784e63d-58ba-553a-8287-ebb64594c0a5" :answer/id #uuid "1784e63d-58ba-553a-8287-ebb64594c0a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-119bb1ed-0657-5ae4-90f2-e955e4848fbc" :answer/id #uuid "119bb1ed-0657-5ae4-90f2-e955e4848fbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1e30d664-9e23-51db-b1eb-ca432067421a" :question/id #uuid "1e30d664-9e23-51db-b1eb-ca432067421a" :question/math-academy-id "q-61245" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-3,-2)$  and $(-6,-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/f7/f7cb9df60327d9a1efa584c5baa6efe6bbf90547d11f87d5e6bad6e535829ea9.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/bd/bd164630f8e4f4e43b02f946bd475789a234b02c80818b57f5112f4535d1a242.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/cc/cc49e78127fd3f35b95fdeb11d70548555ae4efe68fff6d1c355c8fe1591b803.png)\n\nThe point $(-3,-2)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(-6,-2)$ is at a distance of $6$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $6-3=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-406211cc-3e33-5651-8019-7ff90a80e8ba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-406211cc-3e33-5651-8019-7ff90a80e8ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "406211cc-3e33-5651-8019-7ff90a80e8ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3a150c2d-487c-5cc3-95c7-f8288e4d3cfb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b2ecf37-2f30-5cef-aaec-8ca256d8a0bd" "answer-3a150c2d-487c-5cc3-95c7-f8288e4d3cfb" "answer-bfa1cbcd-59f5-51cc-ae36-192035935426" "answer-1f2fddf8-ae4f-5bbb-b1e6-7ed1659ee1b1" "answer-aac91347-75d1-5a5d-bd79-0e9e942729c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b2ecf37-2f30-5cef-aaec-8ca256d8a0bd" :answer/id #uuid "0b2ecf37-2f30-5cef-aaec-8ca256d8a0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answ