wo points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/74/74e3e8f0f4f221f016f0894fb2720f98075c9769f1c4fb3cad9aac9042e05cb6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/51/512d556f62388e66e7fa0ecaf2be7f73cf973e07d641fd37e901d354a11257b1.png)\n\nThe point $(-5,-7)$ is at a distance of $7$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-5,-3)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $7-3=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b42f1b9c-fdac-53cf-8a66-7baeb416267b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b42f1b9c-fdac-53cf-8a66-7baeb416267b" :answer-field/id #uuid "b42f1b9c-fdac-53cf-8a66-7baeb416267b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-17f756d2-a12d-5edc-8e8f-fa2b2bc421c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2bbd542-254a-563d-84f1-ccb7cc846905" "answer-f615d7e6-82ae-5494-8759-b894c591da03" "answer-17f756d2-a12d-5edc-8e8f-fa2b2bc421c4" "answer-78960523-aa5e-59bb-ad93-2f1d20c68677" "answer-ede49085-eb75-5bbf-a865-6a057e8e7419"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2bbd542-254a-563d-84f1-ccb7cc846905" :answer/id #uuid "d2bbd542-254a-563d-84f1-ccb7cc846905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f615d7e6-82ae-5494-8759-b894c591da03" :answer/id #uuid "f615d7e6-82ae-5494-8759-b894c591da03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17f756d2-a12d-5edc-8e8f-fa2b2bc421c4" :answer/id #uuid "17f756d2-a12d-5edc-8e8f-fa2b2bc421c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78960523-aa5e-59bb-ad93-2f1d20c68677" :answer/id #uuid "78960523-aa5e-59bb-ad93-2f1d20c68677" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ede49085-eb75-5bbf-a865-6a057e8e7419" :answer/id #uuid "ede49085-eb75-5bbf-a865-6a057e8e7419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c563b17-7efa-524a-b66b-42f86b7b1c69" :question/id #uuid "1c563b17-7efa-524a-b66b-42f86b7b1c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-161664" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-2,-3)$  and $(3,-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/ee/ee8513d91777bf74afdfd8589f6f234a1b7101aae75c4e36164a01d09d0aa124.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $5$ units, so the distance equals $5.$\n\n![](images/45/45f3c5d8f1bcab9bb4d970df6d3b9996cd14b16cec813ad9243678425d51bdf5.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/fa/fad5095f95dbaa8be864c8d455eb5ef987562ea088c8e7bf14b21f14ca69da24.png)\n\nThe point $(-2,-3)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(3,-3)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $2+3=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27020afd-7c54-5a5f-bc28-335810a08abe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27020afd-7c54-5a5f-bc28-335810a08abe" :answer-field/id #uuid "27020afd-7c54-5a5f-bc28-335810a08abe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5bb3513-6556-50cb-b158-d4abd4051efc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-888490ef-04d2-5076-8ff7-2f1e95e998ca" "answer-3e426b51-3cc5-5e04-bbf2-66229b03631d" "answer-fc